  "body": "## Verification record and remaining gates\n\nDepends on #390 (DM read/API boundary) and #391 (web account-cache isolation). This documentation-only follow-up preserves the final evidence without interrupting #390's in-flight backend CI. Leave draft, unmerged and undeployed.\n\n- Full local Stack build/tests, including the final incremental run: **2,542 examples, zero failures**, exit 0. Source and log hashes recorded.\n- Actual bearer HTTP/PostgreSQL: **93 examples, zero failures**; 1,440 model-derived SQL observations; 9,648-state read model and three specific negative controls.\n- Complete-schema fixtures passed on native PostgreSQL 16.10 and Docker 17.10. Retains the initial child CI startup failure and the TCP-readiness repair; no assertions were weakened.\n- #391's final implementation checks passed at `8b7daf9c81da8e2c1d1fe8f785371fb33d174078`: 28 focused tests locally, lint/application typecheck, hosted social/UI/persona/contracts checks. Scoped-out jobs are not counted as passes.\n- #390 social CI passed at `44a1c7bededf0ba4b54068d482667ac24299f8e4`. Its full backend CI was still running at this snapshot; it is not marked passed. The earlier `02755bc41` full run was superseded/cancelled.\n\nUpdates the source audit, policy matrix and handoff with actual PR dependencies and remaining blockers. No code, migration, flags, deployments or product experiment changes. Full-platform completion remains incomplete: profiles/search/notifications/media, delegated entities/lifecycle/moderation, pagination/native journeys, representative DM performance and useful-outcome instrumentation are still required. The earlier automatic-provider deployment exception remains disclosed.\n",
